# Web structure (`apps/web/src/`)

Mirror the API: features live in `domains/<domain>/`, everything else is shared shell.

- `domains/<domain>/` — one folder per feature (auth, tenant, account, task, marketing):
  - `api.ts` — typed calls for this domain (wraps `@/lib/api`); the only place that builds this domain's endpoints
  - `<name>-provider.tsx` — domain context/state when needed (e.g. auth, tenant)
  - `pages/XxxPage.tsx` — route-level screens (PascalCase, one per file)
  - `routes.tsx` — the domain's routes; **every domain with pages has one** (see routing below)
  - domain-specific components live here too (kebab-case)
  - A domain may import another domain's `api`/provider, but keep it minimal
  - Public marketing screens (landing, pricing…) live in `domains/marketing/`
- `app/` — application shell: `App.tsx` (route map), `config.ts` (app-level config), `NotFoundPage.tsx`
- `layouts/` — AppLayout, AuthLayout, RequireAuth
- `components/ui/` — shadcn (don't hand-rewrite); `components/` — shared app components (below)
- `lib/` — pure infra: `api.ts` (raw HTTP client + `ApiError` + `showApiError`), `utils.ts` (`cn`, `initials`); no domain knowledge
- Network calls go through a domain `api.ts`, never `fetch`/`@/lib/api` directly from a page
- Always import with the `@/` alias (→ `src/`)

## Page template (follow it for every internal page)

Reads use `useQuery`; writes use `useMutation` and invalidate on success. No manual `useState`
loading flags for data. Copy `domains/task/pages/TasksPage.tsx` — it is the canonical example.

- Reads: `useQuery({ queryKey: [resource, tenant.id], queryFn: () => api.list(tenant.id) })`
- Writes: `useMutation({ mutationFn, onSuccess: invalidate, onError: (e) => showApiError(e, "...") })`
- Open with `<PageHeader title description />`; render `<PageLoading />` while `isLoading`; render
  `<EmptyState>` when a list is empty
- Destructive actions use `const confirm = useConfirm()` → `if (await confirm({ title, destructive: true }))`, never `window.confirm`
- Errors from mutations always go through `showApiError(err, fallback)`

## Shared components (`components/`) — reach for these before writing new UI

`PageHeader`, `PageLoading`, `EmptyState`, `RoleSelect`, and `useConfirm`/`ConfirmProvider`
(`confirm-dialog.tsx`). If a UI shape repeats across two pages, extract it here.

## Routing

Each domain exports its routes from `routes.tsx`. Top-level route groups (auth, marketing, tenant)
are composed in `app/App.tsx`. Domains rendered **inside the tenant app shell** (task, account)
export their `<Route>` and are composed inside `tenant/routes.tsx` under the `:tenantSlug` layout.
